Still 1.2.0. Two things, both about the screen lock.

The output now carries a noise floor around -70 dBFS: barely there, inaudible under anything else. iOS suspends an app that stops playing, and the listening state is exactly where this app plays nothing for minutes — which is why the tap gesture died about a minute after the screen locked. Whether this is enough is what the Motion panel's longest-gap row is for.

And the level meter reads the floor instead of freezing when capture is off.
